A demo stream may vary grid dimensions and colors while illustrating a shared transformation. Compare each pair as a complete constraint set: record all changed and preserved cells, boundaries, propagation direction, and where filling stops. Do not assume unrelated palette changes mean a different task.

After an incorrect submission, treat the result as evidence against the submitted rule/grid. State internally what assumption failed, revisit demo differences, and change the candidate meaningfully before trying again. Avoid submitting an identical grid repeatedly. Binary feedback doesn't identify the correct cell, so use the existing demonstrations to narrow alternatives; spend remaining demo requests only when a new example can discriminate among live hypotheses.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1790545211/attempts/88b7a24e5cc74e81b4e76ed1e990732f/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/arc-grid-reasoning/references/binary-feedback-and-mixed-demos.md"}

